answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2722381f-88ef-56ef-a90e-bfc76e1d1ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459685} :answer-field/id #uuid "8af4482e-9012-5e8b-8245-fe732b4fca3e" :answer-field/key "Z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d88d3c9d-ec93-5bf2-a49b-0b326607c0ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-181441" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\sqrt{-1}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-1}=\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\in C.\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-1}$ is nonzero, it does not belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\notin N,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Z,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Q,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3123f8ed-a1ca-52b7-8427-2f3b60d9e68a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points That Lie on a Line" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050790 :topic/id #uuid "6734489a-e850-531c-afa4-62b5b9a5d87f" :topic/math-academy-id 95 :