ges/ca/caeed93f57e554d6bf79b8915935261abb39c6fe54cc6d7d349ff60502a96053.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nGraph positions: **I.** upper left; **II.** upper right; **III.** lower left; **IV.** lower right." :question/worked-solution "Graph I is strictly increasing. Graph II has a local minimum and maximum, graph III first decreases to a visible local minimum and then increases, and graph IV is a downward parabola. Thus II, III, and IV fail the horizontal line test; only I is invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "337518a9-39a1-57e3-8686-74a135f7c3d7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Oriented Curves" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048655 :topic/id #uuid "b2c456e2-ef0a-5a75-95da-68bb5f61da4a" :topic/math-academy-id 3356 :topic/title "Simple, Closed, and Oriented Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52dbce36-54c0-52ac-b02a-1a0dcf5281a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460491} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0e4957-fb2d-57b1-b861-533d087a82b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb0e4957-fb2d-57b1-b861-533d087a82b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460492} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe217ebf-4848-5f37-8c0d-c9ae496feff3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461112} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fbecd13-3f32-58ff-9467-3e1801e294d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 175921864