7592186460498} :answer-field/id #uuid "428af3e1-b497-5b2f-9859-602d61c77fc4" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8658a678-c6ba-5ca2-b63b-0885c74173b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-97928" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b0ced561cd98f9cf81c7de42bee7411a39595a9c59f2edaad0121d712dad157.png)\n\nWhich of the following curves is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented.\n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve II is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve III is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve IV is negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048655 :topic/id #uuid "b2c456e2-ef0a-5a75-95da-68bb5f61da4a" :topic/math-academy-id 3356 :topic/title "Simple, Closed, and Oriented Curves"} :activity/title "Simple, Closed, and Oriented Curves" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418052} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418068}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050189 :topic/id #uuid "34f05255-901a-5db2-9431-e0175ef37691" :topic/math-academy-id 3357 :topic/title "Connected and Simply-Connected Regions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2132682-d892-5ab9-bb87-e66b51a6a1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460499} {:answer/id #uuid "d9edf225-47eb-52d9-9236-490f3c6db5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9edf225-47eb-52d9-9236-490f3c6db5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460500} :answer-field/id #uuid "2118d6af-4ef2-578c-b102-d393d2fbeab2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eccde749-8255-5674-80ee-42a42f6cfc7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460501} {:answer/id #uuid "28f51c6d-3184-5852-b549-1e196a451f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eccde749-8255-5674-80ee-42a42f6cfc7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460501} :answer-field/id #uuid "a559e75b-8ff2-5917-899d-8ec81cc20125" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eb5b6d1-21dc-5ca5-a087-32ff42346fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460503} {:answer/id #uuid "91a9ad8c-64bb-544a-9c5b-62d0b2a8b831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91a9ad8c-64bb-544a-9c5b-62d0b2a8b831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460504} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbbd7b3b-6caf-53d2-85d1-760ead766ae3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461118} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be18d6eb-994d-5193-848d-ff043f487efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460505} {:answer/id #uuid "d10a703c-11a3-5f17-b61d-345a7064eb33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be18d6eb-994d-5193-848d-ff043f487efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460505} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd05271-ff7a-5e38-870a-c107d034a080" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72da8c2e-5747-5cf0-addd-5e327ef519dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-98036" :question/problem "![](images/00/0045eda99f40f774d2ef21214522eebb0c53bffee304ba503a9076a7491cc648.png)\n\nWhich of the regions shown above are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains two holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e86471bd-e6c5-5896-af8e-c48e8e06dc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459811} {:answer/id #uuid "0ae10483-1250-5ee8-a5b7-56019635b6ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e86471bd-e6c5-5896-af8e-c48e8e06dc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459811} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3e684d-5745-5881-b7a9-0cb4fc6b3e66" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ae8346-7f12-51b2-8e39-86863fc03e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459813} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7012c9-36fc-589a-9d2d-cf11e2f8491f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85ae8346-7f12-51b2-8e39-86863fc03e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459813} :answer-field/id #uuid "d610899c-18de-528a-ad41-0903543b7fb2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b69ec572-d020-59f8-83a0-b46528d98a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459815} {:answer/id #uuid "54b24640-ac48-5b77-ab4e-3e63e4bf019d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b69ec572-d020-59f8-83a0-b46528d98a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459815} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a6b85af-a931-557d-a8f0-f8d4434ad92c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "028630ef-e1bc-5d42-ac61-af7d94939f1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34318" :question/problem "![](images/eb/ebeebae27d24ae4dd342b9cf65f93fe58e77aa8dcd99a7cde0880f68378862fa.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside given subset. But\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside given subset. But\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace since in does not contain the zero-vector.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192782 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a8dbbab-2dea-5fff-86f0-3411f5405ee9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Three-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "619d88ad-a1c7-5b3d-8c24-b6a78974ec7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459847} {:answer/id #uuid "543df3d1-82cc-50ab-9e90-e99e3210da09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "619d88ad-a1c7-5b3d-8c24-b6a78974ec7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459847} :answer-field/id #uuid "adf642b5-0d99-5a3e-8aa9-2b628925bcd1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c18b93bd-bcdd-50e4-afa3-95fee527dc67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459849} {:answer/id #uuid "41400ea3-a328-570f-81df-c3348d63b6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41400ea3-a328-570f-81df-c3348d63b6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459850} :answer-field/id #uuid "56504409-bf23-53eb-a559-4baad15a7cde" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192fb319-480e-5a3f-bc8b-a5bec8b0c334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459851} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e8fcbf-9d24-5fd5-ae32-89e8ef38aa0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "192fb319-480e-5a3f-bc8b-a5bec8b0c334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459851} :answer-field/id #uuid "fca5cf1d-3106-5e01-b467-cfe14762ca39" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99d3ff8e-37f2-5365-be21-7d8861823943" :question/math-academy-id "q-35595" :question/problem "![](images/df/df3b62554600601401d14d3b6758a3c350cf8cddc3788e79a3ba456a5a19c60a.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents the origin $0=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,,\\,$ which is considered a special (trivial) subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4dee31d-47c2-5b56-8cea-22d42f7b9de2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric and Antisymmetric Relations From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050493 :topic/id #uuid "4db2b54f-79ed-566a-a082-ccbcb95e93a8" :topic/math-academy-id 4821 :topic/title "Symmetric and Antisymmetric Relations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f991e8f8-3549-51b7-8f46-a4f179c9e60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462237} {:answer/id #uuid "430e2dd1-7999-5f15-afe8-311016bcad2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "430e2dd1-7999-5f15-afe8-311016bcad2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462238} :answer-field/id #uuid "350403e0-9726-5cab-b456-3642d421c3e4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c6b181-ec83-5978-b96f-c05bd5fa6026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462239} {:answer/id #uuid "450492a6-bd5c-51c7-b747-45d35fdc4a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c6b181-ec83-5978-b96f-c05bd5fa6026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462239} :answer-field/id #uuid "be16f79d-a666-5425-8685-2229c8dc678d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462873} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d3452bf-da3c-501c-9084-9b3c0d559be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462241} {:answer/id #uuid "d82344f8-5918-5907-a948-a6d6d2add8cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d3452bf-da3c-501c-9084-9b3c0d559be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462241} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e9a683-a17d-579c-833c-8bcb7bc62ef7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8e6d9019-7f0e-55d6-8ba5-3c61199bf5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-213311" :question/problem "![](images/fd/fdbcfe164fcca0e005255de10f10c10bedc156f3a582eeb5800322d4c4ebe0ab.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent symmetric relations defined on the set $A={0,2,4}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn terms of a plot, if a point $(x,y)$ belongs to the plot, then $(y,x),$ the point symmetric to $(x,y)$ over the diagonal line $y=x,$ should also be on the plot.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nSo, only one of the points, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be on the plot of an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows points on the diagonal line $y=x.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's draw the diagonal line $y=x$ and examine our plots.\n\n![](images/9c/9c9c16300cfb95a61a261e39db865d5c6d056794bd7aaa422567bde10dd4abf5.png)\n\n \n\n- Plot I represents a symmetric relation since the plot is symmetric over the line $y=x.$\n\n- Plot II represents an antisymmetric relation since the plot contains at most one point from each pair of the points symmetric over the line $y=x.$\n\n- Plot III represents neither a symmetric nor an antisymmetric relation. It's not symmetric since, for example, the pair $(4,2)$ belongs to the plot while the point $(2,4)$ does not. And it's not antisymmetric since it contains the pairs $(0,4)$ and $(4,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a0350be-e06b-5da0-8286-d79d466cdbcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437518} {:answer/id #uuid "f9aa62de-aa91-56bb-92b5-f32e48bd2a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a0350be-e06b-5da0-8286-d79d466cdbcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437518} :answer-field/id #uuid "e81cbb98-fd55-5674-8ffd-b8f5364c7566" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "616cf911-5cca-58c7-aad0-375b7975a364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437520} {:answer/id #uuid "fa46cb13-84d3-589c-bce7-1426b00cb3cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "616cf911-5cca-58c7-aad0-375b7975a364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437520} :answer-field/id #uuid "332f37fd-7255-5cb7-a8df-a6fd84707ad4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438789} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27988913-cc9c-5851-8088-a4fc4b07025c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437522} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad7502a-76db-51b2-ab1c-810e56d61640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ad7502a-76db-51b2-ab1c-810e56d61640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437523} :answer-field/id #uuid "872fa28f-f3f6-529b-b025-3590a2dbec87" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5475e656-b1d4-5bfd-b6f4-46f7fafdc2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437524} {:answer/id #uuid "106d9768-5715-5dac-af04-f0b6918d6050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5475e656-b1d4-5bfd-b6f4-46f7fafdc2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437524} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae75796-57c8-5a22-9fb5-6a059099c71c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dda73782-2027-59b5-9ca3-37b046a17959" :question/math-academy-id "q-108581" :question/problem "![](images/89/89b0be0ca7ae1a6e76d32bfc669d6f554deaaad2055b2875e3f6a49821043205.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/cf/cfb095836b7498c91a5cbd9d2cb694715a0d89a12a5e6ea5ff417342c4bde798.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that:\n\n- For graph III, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graph III shows a one-to-one function. As a result, this function is invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, II, and IV, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. These are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4149ef3f-74da-5a1a-9c28-c1d8593e3ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437526} {:answer/id #uuid "f842b5cb-cf9f-52db-975f-f671411d8fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4149ef3f-74da-5a1a-9c28-c1d8593e3ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437526} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3063764-2764-5367-acd1-4008cf7a83c1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438792} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc8acbc6-24a3-5fe2-8e8f-0aea2c2bb813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value