r-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0e004a8-576b-5fb6-94f2-3e66cfd74da8" :question/math-academy-id "q-98338" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1b6a9fa72404e765796d75fc7ba00a391317ef2670e2f65f7c43db32207e8d2.png)\n\nWhich of the curves above is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is not closed.\n\n- Curve II is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve III is a simple and closed curve but it is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve IV is not simple.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050189 :topic/id #uuid "34f05255-901a-5db2-9431-e0175ef37691" :topic/math-academy-id 3357 :topic/title "Connected and Simply-Connected Regions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fffacc9e-beec-5b87-a6ad-4054725f30a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469934} {:answer/id #uuid "5a491a09-f7b0-54c0-8c16-31aefd05fbc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759