answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b01d9637-3916-5456-83d5-9644992bb85b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469940} {:answer/id #uuid "950b233d-c663-5478-b3de-db1d19d6b842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b01d9637-3916-5456-83d5-9644992bb85b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469940} :answer-field/id #uuid "84cbe606-0544-50d5-b199-a029d91a2906" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0317a51a-f6d5-582a-aa69-b3f89cc6775d" :question/math-academy-id "q-98690" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0db1568fab302ddbd9f16dbdf9c276eeb62cbac37346b077c1639fe68c2396ac.png)\n\nWhich of the regions shown above are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions:  \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "281873c8-e173-5181-8281-96b84d636b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Chinese Remainder Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050806 :topic/id #uuid "6836dab1-64c7-50b1-a352-66ffe2ee2572" :topic/math-academy-id 2809 :topic/title "The Chinese Remainder Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbbe17e2-2245-5b19-baca-5456adac09aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471765} {:answer/id #uuid "08a66943-735d-5f31-9404-bb573f0d4a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbbe17e2-2245-5b19-baca-5456adac09aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471765} :answer-field/id #uuid "deb55755-746d-562f-9818-8bd362ec525c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33afde02-6c00-5acc-b627-671a3dd3be13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471767} {:answer/id #uuid "30552bbd-ad0a-50b5-ab48-2ca1fc8d73e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30552bbd-ad0a-50b5-ab48-2ca1fc8d73e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471768} :answer-field/id #uuid "0554ea35-bbf0-5e21-bd1a-586d4cd5d745" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472389} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e90c9bb9-0a65-5aa4-92c8-378c3f722004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471769} {:answer/id #uuid "5231270d-8208-54ce-9a8e-aedfc4af4fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e90c9bb9-0a65-5aa4-92c8-378c3f722004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471769} :answer-field/id #uuid "82ef0c81-c876-58a1-8875-d6aaea32054e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b00b20e-2b69-5a9e-a153-226cf102bd50" :question/math-academy-id "q-83978" :question/problem "According to the Chinese remainder theorem, which of the following systems of congruences has a unique solution modulo $48?$ \n\n$$\n\\text{I.}\\,{\\begin{aligned}x≡4 & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\ x≡5 & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{II.}\\,{\\begin{aligned}x≡2 & (\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ x≡14 & (\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{III.}\\,{\\begin{aligned}x≡3 & (\\text{mod}\\,4) \\\\ x≡7 & (\\text{mod}\\,12)\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Chinese remainder theorem states that if the natural numbers ${n}_{1},{n}_{2},…,{n}_{k}$ are pairwise coprime, meaning that $\\text{gcd}({n}_{i},{n}_{j})=1$ whenever $i\\ne j,$ then for any integers ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},…,{a}_{k}$ the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x≡{a}_{1} & (\\text{mod}\\,{n}_{1}) \\\\ x≡{a}_{2} & (\\text{mod}\\,{n}_{2}) \\\\ \\,⋮ \\\\ x≡{a}_{k} & (\\text{mod}\\,{n}_{k})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nhas a unique solution modulo ${n}_{1}{n}_{2}⋯{n}_{k}.$\n\nLet's now inspect each of the given systems in turn.\n\n- The theorem does *not* apply to system I since $6$ and $8$ are not coprime: \n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(6,8)=2>1\n$$\n\n- The theorem applies to system II. The numbers $3,$ and $16$ are pairwise coprime natural numbers. Therefore, according to the Chinese remainder theorem, the system has a unique solution modulo $3\\cdot 16=48.$\n\n- The theorem does *not* apply to system III since $4$ and $12$ are not coprime: \n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(4,12)=4>1\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "337518a9-39a1-57e3-8686-74a135f7c3d7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Oriented Curves" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048655 :topic/id #uuid "b2c456e2-ef0a-5a75-95da-68bb5f61da4a" :topic/math-academy-id 3356 :topic/title "Simple, Closed, and Oriented Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "666f635f-2d2c-58d1-a88c-b86e8e2df780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471795} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ac7c63-65b4-5309-ae76-0fdcf97d72bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "666f635f-2d2c-58d1-a88c-b86e8e2df780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/valu