:answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471801} {:answer/id #uuid "967dfc80-0ccd-54fc-9cd0-0b3759c0ba32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceb6c668-d138-5653-b3ab-7e1933dee240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471801} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c5a7337-e66d-5281-80a2-b1471a252037" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f035c68d-f32c-5e67-98cc-62c8475830d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-98341" :question/problem "![](images/05/05e7d61ebc2cc2b3d36915d448f6d9a6498376b858f72294f2ffc9342af38a7a.png)\n\nWhich of the curves above is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is not closed.\n\n- Curve II is not simple.\n\n- Curve III is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve IV is a simple and closed curve but it is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28