that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\nFrom the above, we see that in each of the four given graphs, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. Therefore, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, none of them correspond to an invertible function."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048123 :topic/id #uuid "80ecc4ad-075a-51a6-a1fc-72dc61a2444d" :topic/math-academy-id 313 :topic/title "Global vs. Local Extrema and Critical Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4d23575-4aa4-50b3-8f45-fa5b80561dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473154} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8e14b7-e1aa-5f72-99fe-d0d63eed18da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d23575-4aa4-50b3-8f45-fa5b80561dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473154} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f3e8587-e9da-5d96-9590-a8b34259c744" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da106867-9f71-5223-9c5f-fb348c0ba25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473156} {:answer/id #uuid "18fa81c5-1bb2-5ca5-b7a9-e4e88f535b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921