5485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d080acd-916c-5650-8a33-fa75e4ad9891" :question/math-academy-id "q-66509" :question/problem "![](images/be/be5b7625ad6f540f6769b121f52ccad69b669dbf764fc3bb68f89c99f066f145.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/bf/bfc7d94de67ceeb0c4aaa0988c117fce7f15242c2f3d223eecd8f0eb77135d7e.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that: \n\n- For graph IV, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graph IV shows a one-to-one function. This means that  the function is invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, II and  III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459ca46e-eefb-5abd-9d1f-bfc45ab98061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438398} {:answer/id #uuid "035c1b02-9d7f-5f89-80c1-6ac8547e9e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "459ca46e-eefb-5abd-9d1f-bfc45ab98061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer