er/id #uuid "25db3510-d2ea-59b7-a47b-63dc65eb24c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b21044ff-3035-50a3-b828-93a4ae2dde70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472848} :answer-field/id #uuid "e06faf13-f34b-5712-a464-83a6b07e81f1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "085a10d3-7324-5921-95c5-eaa8f395984a" :question/math-academy-id "q-183620" :question/problem "$$\n∀{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $k$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n∀{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,n+{k}^{2}\\ge k\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $k$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∀k$ that uses $k:$\n\n$$\n∀k\\in (0,1),\\,\\overbrace{n+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}^{\\text{scope of }∀k}\n$$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∀\\,{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"} :activity/title "Nested Quantifiers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407113} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407136}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "579250e5-9a15-54a1-9aef-61843d7e73bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472850} {:answer/id #uuid "bac29f65-92c2-5c70-9ac1-938b9b7c9f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "579250e5-9a15-54a1-9aef-61843d7e73bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472850} :answer-field/id #uuid "da4eca5f-8cd7-542e-9644-037ddfda06a8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a3dc152-a2ec-569a-8cdb-75853d4eab7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472852} {:answer/id #uuid "46ef506f-4104-5a21-ad5f-afc0dd168aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46ef506f-4104-5a21-ad5f-afc0dd168aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472853} :answer-field/id #uuid "905f7199-6958-58e0-ad1d-a6857970bc53" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f281ae76-653f-5d18-a0eb-0fe9727b9b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472854} {:answer/id #uuid "6040f888-8437-5a2a-ad58-c9c0b0b28a5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f281ae76-653f-5d18-a0eb-0fe9727b9b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472854} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b222a4-df9e-5d6c-8b68-583b11d65aa7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39d9d2c3-0d6e-5d14-b069-fbe9f014d46f" :question/math-academy-id "q-183674" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $x$ is *bound* since it is placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $y$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃y$ that uses $y:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∀x\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,\\overbrace{x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}^{\\text{scope of }∃y})\n$$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"} :activity/title "Nested Quantifiers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407113} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407135}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7adad79-7530-548f-8ef5-d7d669e56a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473314} {:answer/id #uuid "3e638fd2-f5b6-56e4-a961-6af8957d8b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e638fd2-f5b6-56e4-a961-6af8957d8b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473315} :answer-field/id #uuid "a473b682-7626-5413-963d-7ed5605a64f2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f30a22a7-4bfd-5473-b723-c45d77507594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473316} {:answer/id #uuid "09191b98-cda3-5c87-82cd-aa5bca0c44ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f30a22a7-4bfd-5473-b723-c45d77507594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473316} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a18be48-97e8-5987-8dfc-ecda00586f8b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66355ab9-c052-5d61-9dd1-e8de20763389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473318} {:answer/id #uuid "f502b7b1-cfd1-55bc-bf4e-4a5fb1dfba9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66355ab9-c052-5d61-9dd1-e8de20763389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473318} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a32fca9-dae5-5c00-9560-d1306e445f41" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82f2815d-a760-5a7e-b3a4-18ea182996e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74214" :question/problem "![](images/42/42e0a9a9e987c1c56a335f29cf939e4f03d496fad148f148c32377893dbe7c13.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.  \n\n- Diagram I is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram II represents a line that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so the line in Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. There are vectors  $a=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$  in the subset for which ${a}_{1}>0$ and ${a}_{2}>0.$   But then\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}-{a}_{1} \\\\ -{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space" :topic/_